# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have. All of them are optional:
# without DEEPSEEK_API_KEY the AI chat streams a scripted tutor answer, without
# PISTON_URL runs are simulated by the mock runner, and without DATABASE_URL the
# db:* scripts use the docker-compose.dev.yml defaults below.

# Enables the real tutor (otherwise the chat pane shows a "demo" badge).
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# The dev database from docker-compose.dev.yml (pnpm db:up). Leave it unset to
# use exactly this value; compose substitutes from .env, not from .env.local, so
# changing the port means changing it in both places.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5441/dsa_software

# The code-execution engine. Setting this is what turns real judging on: with it
# unset, Run and Submit are answered by the deterministic mock and the console
# shows a "simulated" badge. The mock never marks a problem solved, so the value
# below is the one you want on a local install — it is also the default the
# `pnpm piston:*` scripts talk to, but that default does not turn judging on.
# PISTON_URL=http://127.0.0.1:2001

# `mock` forces simulated verdicts even with an engine configured — useful for
# exercising a console state without writing code for it. Any other value defers
# to PISTON_URL, which is the default.
# RUNNER_KIND=

# Per-case limits for a real run. The defaults match the ceiling the compose
# service advertises; raising them is what a slower machine needs, not a fix.
# PISTON_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=2000
# PISTON_RUN_MEMORY_MB=256
# PISTON_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4

# The visualizer's own budget, which is a different job from judging a case: a
# trace is megabytes, and every step costs bytes on the engine's stdout and in
# the browser. Steps stop the trace; bytes make the tracer shorten it before the
# engine's buffer does. Raising these needs PISTON_OUTPUT_MAX_SIZE raised in
# docker-compose.dev.yml too, and the piston service recreated (pnpm piston:up).
# PISTON_TRACE_MAX_STEPS=500
# PISTON_TRACE_MAX_BYTES=3500000
# PISTON_TRACE_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=4000

# The engine's own port, used by `pnpm piston:*` and by the compose service. It
# is 2001 rather than Piston's default 2000 to stay clear of other containers.
# PISTON_PORT=2001

# Override where the editor loads Monaco from. Defaults to the self-hosted
# copy at /monaco/vs, generated by scripts/sync-monaco.mjs.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MONACO_VS_URL=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/monaco-editor@0.56.0/min/vs
